WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:03.575
The program's design comes
from Book 4: two policies.

2
00:00:03.575 --> 00:00:07.975
One blocks workloads from anywhere
except their named egress ranges.

3
00:00:07.975 --> 00:00:12.137
The other blocks them when Microsoft's
risk detection marks them high.

4
00:00:12.137 --> 00:00:15.306
They roll out report-only
first, then ring by ring,

5
00:00:15.306 --> 00:00:17.762
and they're never deleted on rollback.

6
00:00:17.762 --> 00:00:19.250
Two decisions frame it.

7
00:00:19.250 --> 00:00:22.950
The licensing decision covers
the top-tier single-tenant apps.

8
00:00:22.950 --> 00:00:26.270
The enforcement decision
is the security chief's:

9
00:00:26.270 --> 00:00:29.913
enforce, wait longer, or
enforce with dated exclusions.

10
00:00:29.913 --> 00:00:32.976
And don't worry when the
risk policy reports nothing;

11
00:00:32.976 --> 00:00:35.880
that's normal until
something is actually risky.
